    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": " \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 153\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 7388, entitled:\n \n    \"AN ACT to amend the labor law, in relation to enacting the \"remedi-\n      al construction of New York labor law act\"\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  The  bill  would  direct courts to interpret the Labor Law in favor of\nworkers.\n \n  I am a champion of New York's workers  and  have  consistently  prior-\nitized  creating  good  jobs,  supporting unions, increasing safety, and\nproviding financial relief for working New Yorkers. New York's Labor Law\nis carefully constructed to  balance  the  interests  of  employers  and\nemployees,  to  ensure that New York's workers are protected, businesses\nare protected from unfair competition, and our state continues to  pros-\nper.  To  the  extent  that  the  Legislature has concerns that specific\nprovisions of the Labor Law are  being  misinterpreted  or  need  to  be\nchanged  to  better protect workers, we should together review and amend\nsuch provisions, rather  than  enact  a  vague  and  sweeping  statutory\nmandate  as  this bill contemplates, putting a thumb on the scale in the\ncontext of disputes.\n \n  Therefore, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                       (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
